  "title": "Quibdó, Chocó (SkySat, post-event) — 10 August 2026",
  "description": "Very-high-resolution (~0.66 m) SkySat collects acquired 10 August 2026 at 19:56 UTC, about seven hours after the mainshock, over Quibdó — the capital of Chocó and the largest population centre in the affected department, roughly 105 km north-northwest of the epicentre. Visual and pansharpened products for building-level and infrastructure damage assessment. Both collects carry ~36% cloud. 2 scenes; each Item carries the available visual, pansharpened assets.",
